# WoW-Style Controls Specification

This file is the source of truth for all input and camera behaviour.
Do NOT change any of these rules without explicit user approval.

---

## Mouse buttons

| Situation | Camera | Character facing | Cursor |
|-----------|--------|-----------------|--------|
| Nothing held | stationary | keeps own facing | visible, free |
| LMB held + mouse still | stationary | keeps own facing | visible, free |
| LMB held + mouse moving | orbits freely around character | keeps own facing (character does NOT rotate with camera) | hides while moving, reappears immediately on release |
| RMB held + mouse still | stationary | keeps own facing | visible |
| RMB held + mouse moving | rotates; character rotates with it (AlwaysFaceYaw=true) | follows camera yaw | hides while moving, reappears immediately on release |
| Both LMB+RMB held | same as RMB + auto-forward | follows camera yaw | hides while rotating |

**Cursor hide rule**: cursor hides only when the mouse has moved past the drag threshold (~20 px) while a button is held. It reappears **immediately** when the button is released, not on the next click.

---

## Keyboard

| Key | Action |
|-----|--------|
| W / Up arrow | move forward |
| S / Down arrow | move backward |
| A | strafe left (always, no mode toggle) |
| D | strafe right (always, no mode toggle) |
| Q / Left arrow | rotate camera left; character follows (AlwaysFaceYaw=true) |
| E / Right arrow | rotate camera right; character follows (AlwaysFaceYaw=true) |
| Space | jump |
| 1 / 2 / 3 | cast Spell1 / Spell2 / Spell3 |
| R | randomise character colour (debug) |

**AlwaysFaceYaw** is set when: RMB held, Q/E/arrows rotating, or A/D strafing.
It is NOT set when only LMB is held (camera orbits but character keeps own facing).

---

## Target selection

| Action | Result |
|--------|--------|
| Tab | cycle through alive Targetable objects (skip local player) |
| LMB quick click (no drag) on Targetable | select that target |
| LMB click on empty space / non-targetable | keep current target (WoW classic) |
| Escape | clear target |

**Implementation notes**:
- Raycast uses `runner.GetPhysicsScene()` first (Fusion objects), then `Physics.Raycast` fallback (floor etc.)
- Drag threshold 20 px; if dragged, release does NOT fire the raycast
- TargetingController.Update reads IsLmbDragging; ThirdPersonOrbitCamera.LateUpdate clears it on release — order guarantees correct read before clear
